<h1>Privacy</h1>
<p class="last-checked">Updated October 31, 2026</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Hosting.</strong> The site is static files served by <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/about-github-pages" rel="nofollow noopener">GitHub Pages</a>. GitHub receives the normal request data any web server gets, such as your IP address.</li>
<li><strong>Analytics.</strong> We count visits with Cloudflare Web Analytics, which Cloudflare says <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/about/" rel="nofollow noopener">does not collect or use your visitors' personal data</a>. We see totals such as page views and page load times, not who you are.</li>
<li><strong>Search.</strong> The search box uses Pagefind, which runs in your browser against files on this site. What you type is not sent to us.</li>
<li><strong>No forms, accounts or cookies of our own.</strong> The site does not ask for your details and sets no cookies itself.</li>
<li><strong>Links out.</strong> Links go to NHTSA and other sites with their own privacy policies. If affiliate links are ever added (they are off today, see <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a>), a retailer may set its own cookies after you click one.</li>
<li><strong>Contact.</strong> <a href="mailto:{{ site.contact }}">{{ site.contact }}</a></li>
</ul>
